+## Secondary Motion from PMX rigid bodies and joints
 
-A PMX's rigid bodies and six-degree-of-freedom spring joints import as one
-`RigidBodyRig` sub-asset per model, in engine units and axes. Add
-**Rigid Body Physics** to the character's Skinned Model entity and point it
-at that sub-asset — one component, one reference, nothing else to configure,
-because the model's author already tuned every body and joint in their own
-tool.
+A PMX's rigid bodies and six-degree-of-freedom spring joints are converted
+best-effort into one engine-native `SecondaryMotionRig` sub-asset per model.
+The importer normalizes source-specific values into engine units and axes and
+emits diagnostics when a shape, body mode, joint kind, binding, or tuning value
+cannot be represented exactly.
 
-The rig is engine-native data plus intent. At runtime, ADR 0096's isolated
-Rapier bridge creates one solver world per opted-in character, drives
-follow-bone bodies from animation, simulates dynamic bodies and 6-DOF spring
-joints, then writes corrected poses back to the skeleton. These cosmetic
-bodies never enter gameplay collision events or spatial queries.
+Add **Secondary Motion** to the character's Skinned Model entity and assign
+that rig. The component serializes as `engine.secondary_motion` and contains
+only the rig reference. The imported rig is editable engine-native starting
+data, not a promise to reproduce a particular MMD/Bullet solver exactly.
+
+At runtime, ADR 0112's isolated fixed-step solver creates one simulation world
+per opted-in character, drives follow-bone bodies from the procedural pose,
+simulates dynamic bodies and 6-DOF constraints, and writes corrections only to
+the RigPose physics layer. Presentation interpolates fixed-step poses for
+rendering. These cosmetic bodies never enter gameplay collision events or
+spatial queries, and discontinuities reset derived simulation state rather than
+reconstructing hidden animation history.
 
